**My own solution first:**

The problem asks: Chim Tu has 4 T-shirts. An outfit consists of 3 or more T-shirts worn in a specific order. Two outfits are distinct if the sets differ OR the order differs. He changes outfit every 3 days and never repeats. How many days can he survive?

This is asking for the total number of ordered selections (permutations) of 3 or more items from 4 items.

- **Outfits with exactly 3 T-shirts:** This is P(4,3) = 4!/(4-3)! = 4!/1! = 24. (Choose and order 3 from 4.)
- **Outfits with exactly 4 T-shirts:** This is P(4,4) = 4! = 24. (All 4, ordered in all possible ways.)

Total outfits: 24 + 24 = 48.

Days of survival: 48 outfits × 3 days per outfit = 144 days.

